-- title:
--   The different is local at each prime of a Galois extension
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $F$ be number fields with $F$ an extension of $K$ that is Galois, and let $P$ be a height one prime of the ring of integers $\mathcal{O}_F$. Write $A_P \subseteq F$ for the valuation subring of the $P$-adic valuation of $F$; since every element of $\mathcal{O}_F$ has $P$-valuation at most $1$, the structure map $\mathcal{O}_F \to F$ restricts to a ring homomorphism $\mathcal{O}_F \to A_P$. Let $D =$ [`NumberField.PlaceDecomp.decomp K F P`](def/NumberField_PlaceDecompositionAction.html#L82) be the decomposition subgroup of $A_P$ over $K$ inside the group $F \simeq_{\mathrm{alg}[K]} F$ of $K$-algebra automorphisms of $F$, and let $A_P^{D} =$ `FixedPoints.subring` $A_P\, D$ be the subring of $A_P$ fixed by this group action. The assertion is that the ideal of $A_P$ generated by the image of the relative different $\mathfrak{D}_{\mathcal{O}_F/\mathcal{O}_K} =$ `differentIdeal (𝓞 K) (𝓞 F)` under the above homomorphism coincides with the different ideal of the extension $A_P^{D} \subseteq A_P$, i.e. $\mathfrak{D}_{\mathcal{O}_F/\mathcal{O}_K} \cdot A_P = \mathfrak{D}_{A_P/A_P^{D}}$.
--
--   This is the localisation statement that the different is a local invariant: at each prime the global relative different of a Galois extension of number fields agrees with the different of the corresponding local Galois layer given by the decomposition group. It feeds the computation of the exponent of $P$ in the different by Hilbert's formula, and is used in [`NumberField.card_mul_factorization_discr_fixedField_eq_inertiaDeg_mul_finsum_u0`](thm.html#NumberField.card_mul_factorization_discr_fixedField_eq_inertiaDeg_mul_finsum_u0) towards the factorisation of discriminants of fixed fields.
